WEBVTT

01:05:25.750 --> 01:05:30.518
And the story of our lives is a story
of where we wished we had stayed longer

01:05:30.542 --> 01:05:32.518
and where we wished we had left sooner.

01:05:32.542 --> 01:05:35.934
And I don't think
that there is a specific, you know,

01:05:35.958 --> 01:05:40.625
I can say I have rarely heard people
leave a job and regret it.

01:05:41.417 --> 01:05:43.643
But I do look at our time, my dear.

01:05:43.667 --> 01:05:47.018
AG: There's one other quick thing
I wanted to bring up before we wrap,

01:05:47.042 --> 01:05:49.684
which is, we got a bunch
of questions via social media.

01:05:49.708 --> 01:05:52.101
There's this question I love
from Michelle Miller,

01:05:52.125 --> 01:05:55.018
which is, what do we think
about work spouses?

01:05:55.042 --> 01:05:56.309
And I have to tell you --

01:05:56.333 --> 01:05:58.726
I've heard people
use this term increasingly,

01:05:58.750 --> 01:06:00.143
over the last few years.